From 2ed17f579dde0a9cf4a56eb58ed43fb044ff2b0b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rudi Heitbaum <rudi@heitbaum.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 09:26:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] CurlFile: pass the credentials of an FTP source to curl as
 options

ParseAndCorrectUrl() read the user and password of a URL only for http
and https. For ftp and ftps they stayed in the URL alone. Open() then
replaces m_url with CURLINFO_EFFECTIVE_URL, and since curl 8.23.0 (its
commit 7a6bd027d0, "getinfo: make sure CURLINFO_EFFECTIVE_URL does not
contain creds") that URL carries none: a transfer started again from
m_url, as Seek() does, logged in anonymously and the server refused it
("Login denied", 67). An FTP source with a password stopped at the first
seek, for example when the demuxer reads the cues at the end of a
Matroska file. Hades has curl 8.23.0.

The credentials are now read for every protocol, before the protocol's
own handling, and go to curl as CURLOPT_USERNAME and CURLOPT_PASSWORD
for FTP as they did for HTTP. A stale user of an earlier HTTP address is
no longer kept for an FTP one either.

The trailing slash of an FTP path is put back only after a file name:
ftp://user:pass@host// left an empty name and a lone "/", and without the
credentials in m_url (GetWithoutUserDetails()) that is ftp://host//,
the root of the server to curl rather than the directory of the login.

From Rudi Heitbaum's pull request to Kodi, xbmc/xbmc#30391 ("Pass ftp
credentials to curl as options", open at the time), its two commits
68f3539f8796 and 1fbeab6eb069, with the comments rewritten.
---
 xbmc/filesystem/CurlFile.cpp | 16 ++++++++++------
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/xbmc/filesystem/CurlFile.cpp b/xbmc/filesystem/CurlFile.cpp
index dfaa973..76273b9 100644
--- a/xbmc/filesystem/CurlFile.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/filesystem/CurlFile.cpp
@@ -861,6 +861,13 @@ void CCurlFile::ParseAndCorrectUrl(CURL &url2)
       m_dnsCacheList = tempCache;
   }
 
+  // The user and password of every protocol go to curl as options (SetCommonOptions()). Open()
+  // replaces m_url with CURLINFO_EFFECTIVE_URL, which since curl 8.23.0 carries no credentials:
+  // read for http and https only, an FTP source with a password lost them at the first transfer
+  // started again from m_url (a seek), and the server refused the anonymous login.
+  m_username = url2.GetUserName();
+  m_password = url2.GetPassWord();
+
   if( url2.IsProtocol("ftp")
    || url2.IsProtocol("ftps") )
   {
@@ -900,8 +907,9 @@ void CCurlFile::ParseAndCorrectUrl(CURL &url2)
       filename += CURL::Encode(*it);
     }
 
-    /* make sure we keep slashes */
-    if(StringUtils::EndsWith(url2.GetFileName(), "/"))
+    // make sure we keep slashes, but not as a lone "/": without the credentials in m_url,
+    // ftp://host// is the root of the server to curl, not the directory of the login
+    if (!filename.empty() && StringUtils::EndsWith(url2.GetFileName(), "/"))
       filename += "/";
 
     url2.SetFileName(filename);
@@ -950,10 +958,6 @@ void CCurlFile::ParseAndCorrectUrl(CURL &url2)
                   m_proxyhost, proxyType2CUrlProxyType.at(m_proxytype));
     }
 
-    // get username and password
-    m_username = url2.GetUserName();
-    m_password = url2.GetPassWord();
-
     // handle any protocol options
     std::map<std::string, std::string> options;
     url2.GetProtocolOptions(options);
